.TH CHTTPSVR_RESP_PRINTF 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chttpsvr_resp_printf \- format and append a printf-style string to the response body
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/chttpserver.h>

ccol_retval_t chttpsvr_resp_printf(chttpsvr_resp *resp,
                                    const char *fmt, ...);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Formats fmt and the variadic arguments by the printf rules and appends
the result to the response body, which is equivalent to formatting
into a temporary string and passing it to chttpsvr_resp_write_str.
Short output goes through a small internal stack buffer; longer output
falls back to a temporary heap allocation of exactly the size of the
formatted text, which is freed before the function returns.  Repeated
calls append to the same response body, as with
chttpsvr_resp_write_str.

The compiler checks the format string through the GCC attribute
__attribute__((format(printf, 2, 3))).
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success           - The formatted output was appended to the
                         body.
ccol_invalid_args      - resp or fmt is NULL, or the underlying
                          vsnprintf call reports an encoding error.
ccol_not_enough_memory - The body buffer or the temporary heap buffer
                          could not be allocated.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttpsvr_resp_write (3),
.BR chttpsvr_resp_write_str (3),
.BR chttpsvr_resp_write_json (3)
